{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments [{:quotes [{:he "לא תכירו פנים במשפט", :translit "lo takiru panim ba'mishpat", :gloss "you shall not recognize faces in judgment"} {:he "תגין על פ\"א", :translit "tagin al peh", :gloss "tagin on the peh"} {:he "פתח פיך לאלם", :translit "pitech pichea le'ilem", :gloss "open your mouth for the mute"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Tagin drawn on the letter peh signal the phrase 'open your mouth for the mute,' an allusion to Proverbs 31:8."}], :frame {:text "The verse Proverbs 31:8 reads פִּי־פֶּתַח לְאִלֵּם — 'Open your mouth for the mute.' The tagin on the peh visually point the judge to this obligation.", :sources ["Proverbs 31:8"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כקטן הגדול תשמעון", :translit "ka'katon ha'gadol tishme'un", :gloss "as the small the great you shall hear"} {:he "כקטן יהיו בעיניך", :translit "ka'katon yihyu be'enecha", :gloss "as small they should be in your eyes"} {:he "בעוד שעומדים לפניך יהיו בעיניך שניהם כרשעים", :translit "be'od she'omdim lifanecha yihyu be'enecha shneihem ke'resha'im", :gloss "while they stand before you both should be in your eyes like wicked"} {:he "וכשנפטרים מלפניך יהיו בעיניך שניהם כגדולים", :translit "u'che'shenif'tarim mi'lifanecha yihyu be'enecha shneihem ke'g'dolim", :gloss "and when they depart from before you both should be in your eyes like great ones"} {:he "פי' כצדיקים", :translit "pirush ke'tzadikim", :gloss "meaning like righteous"}], :mechanisms [], :frame nil} {:quotes [{:he "תשמעון", :translit "tishme'un", :gloss "you shall hear"} {:he "נביא אקים לך וגו' אליו תשמעון", :translit "navi akim lecha v'gomer elav tishme'un", :gloss "a prophet I will raise for you etc. to him you shall hear"} {:he "כקטן כגדול תשמעון", :translit "ka'katon ka'gadol tishme'un", :gloss "as the small as the great you shall hear"} {:he "דין של נביא ות\"ח", :translit "din shel navi v'ta'am chacham", :gloss "a case of a prophet and a Torah scholar"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["תשמעון" "תשמעון"]}], :frame {:text "The second occurrence is at Deuteronomy 18:15 — נָבִיא אָקִים לָהֶם מִקֶּרֶב אֲחֵיהֶם כָּמוֹךָ וְנָתַתִּי דְבָרַי בְּפִיו וְדִבֶּר אֲלֵיהֶם אֵת כָּל אֲשֶׁר אֲצַוֶּנּוּ. Verse 18:15 continues וְאֵלָיו תִּשְׁמָעוּן — 'to him you shall listen.' Ba'al HaTurim reasons that when a prophet and a Torah scholar face each other in a legal dispute, this second verse grants the prophet priority.", :sources ["Deuteronomy 18:15"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כי המשפט", :translit "ki ha'mishpat", :gloss "for the judgment"} {:he "תגין על הפ\"א", :translit "tagin al ha'peh", :gloss "tagin on the peh"} {:he "כאילו גיהנם פתוחה מתחתיו", :translit "ke'ilu gehinom ptuchah mi'tachato", :gloss "as though Gehenna is open beneath it"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Tagin on the alef of ha'alef in המשפט signal that Gehenna lies open beneath a corrupt judge."}], :frame {:text "The Talmud states that any judge who renders a true verdict causes the Divine Presence to dwell among Israel, while Sanhedrin 7a warns that a judge who perverts justice is called a destroyer of God's world. Gehenna awaits the unjust judge.", :sources ["Sanhedrin 7a" "Shabbat 10a"]}} {:quotes [{:he "כי המשפט לאלהים הוא", :translit "ki ha'mishpat la'elohim hu", :gloss "for the judgment is God's"} {:he "וסמיך ליה והדבר אשר יקשה מכם", :translit "v'samach leih ve'ha'davar asher yikasheh mikem", :gloss "and adjacent to it and the matter that is hard for you"} {:he "כל המקשה ערפו כנגד הדיין כאילו מקשה כנגד השכינה", :translit "kol ha'makasheh arpo keneged ha'dayan ke'ilu makasheh keneged ha'shechinah", :gloss "whoever stiffens his neck against the judge it is as if he stiffens against the Shechinah"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :other, :note "Adjoining verses are read together: the phrase 'for the judgment is God's' directly precedes 'and the matter that is too hard for you,' establishing that rejecting a judge's authority is equivalent to rejecting the Shekhinah."}], :frame {:text "Shabbat 10a states that any judge who judges a true judgment becomes a partner with the Holy One, Blessed be He, in Creation — the verse 'for the judgment is Elohim's' identifies the judicial act as Divine. The immediately adjoining verse, Deuteronomy 1:17 — 'and the matter that is too hard for you, you shall bring to me' — establishes the chain of judicial authority. Deuteronomy 10:16 commands וּמַלְתֶּם אֵת עָרְלַת לְבַבְכֶם וְעָרְפְּכֶם לֹא תַקְשׁוּ עוֹד, 'you shall circumcise the foreskin of your heart and stiffen your neck no more,' providing the idiom of stiffening the neck as rebellion.", :sources ["Shabbat 10a" "Deuteronomy 1:17" "Deuteronomy 10:16"]}} {:quotes [{:he "והדבר", :translit "ve'ha'davar", :gloss "and the matter"} {:he "והדבר הזה לא אוכל לעשות", :translit "ve'ha'davar ha'zeh lo uchal la'asot", :gloss "and this matter I cannot do"} {:he "והדבר אשר דברנו אני ואתה", :translit "ve'ha'davar asher dibarnu ani ve'atah", :gloss "and the matter that we spoke I and you"} {:he "והדבר אשר יקשה מכם", :translit "ve'ha'davar asher yikasheh mikem", :gloss "and the matter that is hard for you"} {:he "שלא ידע מה שידעו בנות צלפחד", :translit "she'lo yadah mah she'yad'u benot tzelofchad", :gloss "that he did not know what the daughters of Zelophehad knew"} {:he "והדבר הזה לא אוכל לעשות", :translit "ve'ha'davar ha'zeh lo uchal la'asot", :gloss "and this matter I cannot do"} {:he "שלא יכול לעשותו", :translit "she'lo yachol la'asoto", :gloss "that he could not do it"} {:he "והדבר אשר דברנו אני ואתה", :translit "ve'ha'davar asher dibarnu ani ve'atah", :gloss "and the matter that we spoke I and you"} {:he "ה' יהיה ביני ובינך וגו'", :translit "Hashem yihyeh beini u'veinecha v'gomer", :gloss "HaShem will be between me and you etc."} {:he "ויקרב משה את משפטן לפני ה'", :translit "va'yakrev Moshe et mishpatan lifnei Hashem", :gloss "and Moses brought their judgment before HaShem"}], :mechanisms [{:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["והדבר" "והדבר הזה לא אוכל לעשות" "והדבר אשר דברנו אני ואתה"]}], :frame {:text "Numbers 27:5 records וַיַּקְרֵב מֹשֶׁה אֶת מִשְׁפָּטָן לִפְנֵי יְהוָה — Moses brought the daughters of Zelophehad's case before God. Numbers 36:2 opens with וַיֹּאמְרוּ… 'and the matter that we spoke, I and you,' followed in verse 36:5 by ה' יהיה ביני ובינכם, linking the judicial outcome to Divine mediation. Deuteronomy 1:12 reads וְהַדָּבָר הַזֶּה לֹא אוּכַל לְעָשׂוֹת לְבַדִּי, where Moses declares he cannot bear the burden of judging alone, corresponding to his inability to resolve cases that demanded direct Divine consultation.", :sources ["Numbers 27:5" "Numbers 36:2" "Numbers 36:5" "Deuteronomy 1:12"]}}], :arithmetic [{:kind :other, :note "Tagin drawn on the letter peh signal the phrase 'open your mouth for the mute,' an allusion to Proverbs 31:8.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 2, :occurrences ["תשמעון" "תשמעון"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "תשמעון", :refs ["Deuteronomy 1:17" "Deuteronomy 7:12" "Deuteronomy 8:20" "Deuteronomy 18:15" "Jeremiah 17:24" "Zechariah 6:15" "Daniel 3:5" "Daniel 3:15"], :n 8, :lens :exact} {:phrase "תשמעון", :refs ["Deuteronomy 1:17" "Deuteronomy 7:12" "Deuteronomy 8:20" "Deuteronomy 18:15" "Jeremiah 17:24" "Zechariah 6:15" "Daniel 3:5" "Daniel 3:15"], :n 8, :lens :exact}]} {:kind :other, :note "Tagin on the alef of ha'alef in המשפט signal that Gehenna lies open beneath a corrupt judge.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :other, :note "Adjoining verses are read together: the phrase 'for the judgment is God's' directly precedes 'and the matter that is too hard for you,' establishing that rejecting a judge's authority is equivalent to rejecting the Shekhinah.", :by :selah, :ran? false} {:kind :masorah, :count 3, :occurrences ["והדבר" "והדבר הזה לא אוכל לעשות" "והדבר אשר דברנו אני ואתה"], :by :selah, :located [{:phrase "והדבר", :refs ["Deuteronomy 1:17" "1 Samuel 20:23" "1 Kings 20:9" "Jeremiah 5:13" "Jeremiah 32:24" "Ezekiel 7:15"], :n 6, :lens :exact} {:phrase "והדבר הזה לא אוכל לעשות", :refs ["1 Kings 20:9"], :n 1, :lens :exact} {:phrase "והדבר אשר דברנו אני ואתה", :refs ["1 Samuel 20:23"], :n 1, :lens :exact}]}], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :baal-haturim, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :discipline "bht-chalkboard-v1", :timestamp "2026-07-12T23:34:40.936048579Z", :model "glm-5.2"}